    "intro_html":  "In New Orleans, red beans and rice is Monday food. Monday was wash day, the pot could sit on the stove unattended all morning, and the ham bone from Sunday went in with the beans. This version seasons ground turkey like Cajun sausage and simmers it with kidney beans, tomatoes, and the holy trinity over rice. Each serving carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Beans and rice have been the best protein-per-dollar math in America for two centuries and nothing has come along to beat it.",
